# Settings for the release train's commands (scripts/train): the ship
# (filex-ship.sh), the merge queue and when-done. Copy to
# ~/.config/filex-train.env (or point FILEX_TRAIN_ENV, or --env, at a file).
# KEY=VALUE, no expansion; the process environment wins over this file.
#
# ⚠ No secret is a value here: a key is the FILE it is in, or the name of the
# variable that holds it. Hosts and paths below are placeholders.

# ── who is told when a long step ends (scripts/lib/notify.mjs) ─────────────
# A person: a JSON POST {group, source, severity, title, message} with a
# Bearer key read from the file. Unset URL = nobody is told this way.
# FILEX_NOTIFY_URL=https://notify.example.com/api/notify/v1/send
# FILEX_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE=/home/you/.config/filex-train/notify.key
# FILEX_NOTIFY_GROUP=infra
# FILEX_NOTIFY_SOURCE=filex-train

# An agent: an MCP server's `notify` tool, once per name in FILEX_WAKE_AGENT
# (comma or space separated; a person's name there reaches that person). An
# agent wakes when its session is waiting on its inbox. The token: a file, or
# the name of a variable the session already holds.
# FILEX_WAKE_URL=https://work.example.com/mcp/work
# FILEX_WAKE_TOKEN_FILE=/home/you/.config/filex-train/wake.token
# FILEX_WAKE_TOKEN_ENV=WORK_MCP_TOKEN
# FILEX_WAKE_AGENT=release-session
# FILEX_WAKE_FROM=filex-train
# FILEX_WAKE_PROJECT=<project id>
# FILEX_WAKE_TASK=<task number in that project>

# ── the ship (scripts/train/ship.mjs) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The server the instances run on, as ssh knows it, and how to reach it.
SHIP_HOST=app-server
# SHIP_SSH_OPTS=-o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=20

# The instances, deployed in this order: the demo first - it is the canary,
# and a failed instance stops the ones after it.
SHIP_INSTANCES=demo prod
SHIP_DEMO_DIR=/srv/filex-demo
SHIP_DEMO_PORT=5212
SHIP_PROD_DIR=/srv/filex
SHIP_PROD_PORT=5213
# Per instance, when not the default: its SQLite file under DIR (none = not
# SQLite: no copy, no migration check), and its compose service.
# SHIP_PROD_DB=data/instance.sqlite
# SHIP_PROD_SERVICE=filex

# The image; where backups go (a new pre-<tag>-<time> directory every
# attempt); seconds /healthz has after a start; what a failed instance gets
# (rollback, or hold: left as it failed).
# SHIP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/brf-tech/filex
# SHIP_BACKUP_ROOT=/var/backups/filex
# SHIP_HEALTH_WAIT=300
# SHIP_ON_FAIL=rollback

# The publishing commands, run here (in Git Bash on Windows). A step whose
# command is not set is left to a person and listed at the end.
# The desktop command gets the directory the release's packages were
# downloaded to; the assets are `gh release download` patterns.
# SHIP_MANIFEST_CMD=bash /path/to/publish-update-manifest.sh
# SHIP_DESKTOP_CMD=bash /path/to/publish-desktop-feed.sh
# SHIP_DESKTOP_ASSETS=latest*.yml filex-desktop-*.exe filex-desktop-*.deb
# The CDN in front of the feed host: a command ON SHIP_HOST that purges URLs,
# and the feed's public base URL the file names are appended to.
# SHIP_PURGE_CMD=bash /path/on/server/purge-urls.sh
# SHIP_FEED_URL=https://downloads.example.com/desktop

# docs site: the source snapshot ON SHIP_HOST and the command there that
# rebuilds and publishes it. Pages come from the public checkout.
# SHIP_DOCS_SRC=/srv/filex-docs-src
# SHIP_DOCS_REFRESH=bash /path/on/server/docs-refresh.sh --force
# SHIP_EXPORT_DIR=/path/to/filex-export
# SHIP_GITHUB_REPO=BRF-Tech/filex

# npm (minutes to wait for every package), then the embedded explorer:
# re-vendor it (and, when set, deploy it).
# SHIP_NPM_WAIT=20
# SHIP_REVENDOR_CMD=bash /path/to/revendor.sh --apply --force
# SHIP_EMBEDS_DEPLOY_CMD=bash /path/to/deploy-embeds.sh

# The language packs are not the ship's: it prints their release-day step,
# `node scripts/langpacks.mjs release X.Y.Z`, which finds the packs itself
# (beside the checkout, or FILEX_LANG_PACKS) - see CONTRIBUTING, Release
# process, step 13.
